1
00:00:00,765 --> 00:00:06,742
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,747 --> 00:00:09,747
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,747 --> 00:00:10,747
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,747 --> 00:00:11,747
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:15,294
[Episode 8]

6
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:18,521
I told you I'm all better.

7
00:00:18,521 --> 00:00:21,957
I was cooped up in a hospital for months.
I just needed to get out.

8
00:00:21,957 --> 00:00:26,289
<i>The doctor said you shouldn't
push yourself for a while.</i>

9
00:00:26,289 --> 00:00:29,105
<i>You've only been out for a few days.
Why go somewhere that rough?</i>

10
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:31,201
Come on, if it were that rough,
I wouldn't have made it here.

11
00:00:31,201 --> 00:00:35,062
The roads are much better these days.
They go all the way up to the lodge...

12
00:00:37,161 --> 00:00:40,037
Oh... Mom, I'm in the mountains,
so the signal is bad.

13
00:00:40,037 --> 00:00:41,200
I'll eat well, get plenty of rest,

14
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,261
and head back in a week,
so don't worry too much.

15
00:00:43,261 --> 00:00:44,961
I'm hanging up now.

16
00:00:52,213 --> 00:00:54,097
Hello! How have you been?

17
00:00:54,097 --> 00:00:55,457
Oh, welcome.

18
00:00:55,457 --> 00:00:56,497
Have you been well?

19
00:00:56,497 --> 00:00:58,845
Oh, careful, it's slippery.

20
00:00:58,845 --> 00:01:00,133
Why are you out in this cold?

21
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:01,529
You've been well, right?

22
00:01:01,529 --> 00:01:05,893
You usually come toward the end of summer.
What brings you here in the winter?

23
00:01:05,893 --> 00:01:09,301
I had some things to take care of,
so it turned out this way.

24
00:01:09,301 --> 00:01:12,961
The road was rough, so you had
a hard time getting up here, huh?

25
00:01:12,961 --> 00:01:14,865
Yeah, it took a little longer than usual.

26
00:01:14,865 --> 00:01:17,385
Oh, you're lucky the weather's good today.

27
00:01:17,385 --> 00:01:19,162
Once it snows, you can't even get up here.

28
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:24,096
In the winter, you can only come and go
if the mountain allows it.

29
00:01:24,096 --> 00:01:27,961
You must be tired.
Go on up, unpack, and get some rest.

30
00:01:27,961 --> 00:01:29,509
Okay, it's the same room
I always stay in, right?

31
00:01:29,509 --> 00:01:30,917
No, the room next door.

32
00:01:30,917 --> 00:01:32,461
That one's occupied.

33
00:01:32,461 --> 00:01:34,161
Occupied?

34
00:01:35,977 --> 00:01:38,513
<i>A young woman came a few days ago.</i>

35
00:01:38,513 --> 00:01:40,953
<i>She seems to have no energy.
She just sleeps all day.</i>

36
00:01:40,953 --> 00:01:42,765
<i>She's always collapsing wherever she is.</i>

37
00:01:42,765 --> 00:01:45,562
<i>Oh, I'm worried sick about her.</i>

38
00:02:33,525 --> 00:02:35,225
Excuse...

39
00:02:43,865 --> 00:02:45,929
<i>Doesn't she remember me?</i>

40
00:02:52,429 --> 00:02:53,429
Good morning!

41
00:02:53,429 --> 00:02:55,417
- Oh, welcome!
- Welcome.

42
00:02:55,417 --> 00:02:57,496
Have a seat.

43
00:02:57,496 --> 00:02:59,229
Alright.

44
00:03:03,149 --> 00:03:04,437
Oh, the woman in the next room?

45
00:03:04,437 --> 00:03:07,465
That young lady doesn't
usually eat breakfast.

46
00:03:07,465 --> 00:03:09,457
It would be a relief
if she just skipped breakfast.

47
00:03:09,457 --> 00:03:12,469
She skips lunch and dinner even more often.

48
00:03:12,469 --> 00:03:15,901
Even when she sits down for a meal,
she barely eats a few bites.

49
00:03:15,901 --> 00:03:17,533
How long is she staying?

50
00:03:17,533 --> 00:03:22,337
She paid a month's room
and meal fees up front, but who knows.

51
00:03:22,337 --> 00:03:26,969
There isn't much to do around here.
She might get bored and leave early.

52
00:03:26,969 --> 00:03:30,281
How long are you staying this time?

53
00:03:30,281 --> 00:03:32,396
Well, I was thinking about a week...

54
00:03:34,441 --> 00:03:38,562
I'm thinking of staying
until I get a little bored of it this time.

55
00:03:42,821 --> 00:03:45,762
Oh, come over here and have a bite with us.

56
00:03:48,189 --> 00:03:49,581
Oh, jeez.

57
00:03:49,581 --> 00:03:51,229
Come on, eat.

58
00:03:51,229 --> 00:03:52,829
Okay.

59
00:03:52,829 --> 00:03:57,481
She's so quiet. Looks like
she's heading back into the mountains.

60
00:03:57,481 --> 00:03:59,765
I don't know where she gets
the energy when she barely eats.

61
00:03:59,765 --> 00:04:03,362
Still, it's better than
sleeping in her room all day.

62
00:04:07,337 --> 00:04:09,793
Don't we have too little meat?

63
00:04:09,793 --> 00:04:11,865
Should we grill some meat for dinner?

64
00:04:11,865 --> 00:04:14,529
Yeah, sounds good.

65
00:04:44,953 --> 00:04:46,653
Huh?

66
00:04:49,489 --> 00:04:50,609
Oh...

67
00:04:50,609 --> 00:04:53,405
Wow, you walk incredibly fast.

68
00:04:53,405 --> 00:04:56,905
I thought you were using
some kind of magic shortcut.

69
00:04:56,905 --> 00:04:59,396
I guess you like hiking, huh?

70
00:05:01,177 --> 00:05:02,962
I'm not usually weak in the legs.

71
00:05:02,962 --> 00:05:06,189
It's just that the terrain
around here is pretty rough.

72
00:05:06,189 --> 00:05:08,349
And I had a pretty serious injury recently,

73
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:10,562
so I spent quite a while in the hospital.

74
00:05:10,562 --> 00:05:13,493
Do you happen to know
Gyeongsan Hospital in Gyeongsan-dong?

75
00:05:13,493 --> 00:05:15,553
Darn it! Ah!

76
00:05:20,821 --> 00:05:24,862
We're having a barbecue tonight.
You have to join us!

77
00:05:27,193 --> 00:05:29,729
Still so aloof.

78
00:05:40,541 --> 00:05:43,129
I see you prefer protein.

79
00:05:44,181 --> 00:05:46,329
Honey, hurry up and grill the meat.
Please grill all of it.

80
00:05:46,329 --> 00:05:50,421
Yeah, we'll have to stock up on meat
next time we go grocery shopping.

81
00:05:57,709 --> 00:06:02,209
By the way, when are you going
to bring your girlfriend?

82
00:06:02,209 --> 00:06:04,801
Don't you get tired of always coming alone?

83
00:06:04,801 --> 00:06:09,762
I haven't met my perfect match
like you two yet.

84
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,769
Honey, the fire's getting low.

85
00:06:12,769 --> 00:06:16,573
I need to get some dry firewood
from the shed.

86
00:06:16,573 --> 00:06:18,541
I'll get it.

87
00:06:18,541 --> 00:06:20,362
Okay, sure.

88
00:06:31,365 --> 00:06:33,362
Give it to me. I'll carry it.

89
00:06:38,429 --> 00:06:41,217
Don't you remember me?
We've met before. Twice.

90
00:06:41,217 --> 00:06:43,053
- Yes, I remember.
- Right?

91
00:06:43,053 --> 00:06:44,929
I knew you'd remember.

92
00:06:44,929 --> 00:06:47,229
Wow, meeting for a third time
all the way out here!

93
00:06:47,229 --> 00:06:50,296
Isn't this an incredible coincidence?

94
00:06:50,296 --> 00:06:52,541
How could something like this happen?

95
00:06:52,541 --> 00:06:54,829
This is such a remote place,
and hardly anyone knows about it.

96
00:06:54,829 --> 00:06:57,725
At this point, I'd say we have
a pretty unusual connection.

97
00:06:57,725 --> 00:06:59,425
Excuse me.

98
00:07:01,133 --> 00:07:02,133
Yes?

99
00:07:02,133 --> 00:07:05,141
I came here
because I don't want to do anything.

100
00:07:05,141 --> 00:07:07,662
- Pardon?
- I just want some peace and quiet.

101
00:07:19,877 --> 00:07:21,862
I'm the one staying in the room next door.

102
00:07:27,005 --> 00:07:30,433
The owners went down
the mountain early this morning.

103
00:07:30,433 --> 00:07:32,562
It's their monthly grocery shopping day.

104
00:07:32,562 --> 00:07:34,833
They asked me to make sure you eat.

105
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:37,496
But you hadn't come down by lunchtime.

106
00:07:38,481 --> 00:07:41,233
I won't ask you to do anything or bother you.

107
00:07:41,233 --> 00:07:43,062
So let's just eat.

108
00:07:43,681 --> 00:07:47,362
Come down whenever you feel like it.
I'll be waiting.

109
00:09:31,693 --> 00:09:33,396
Excuse me!

110
00:09:34,801 --> 00:09:37,696
I think you should come outside for a moment.

111
00:09:38,709 --> 00:09:40,409
Excuse me?

112
00:09:45,053 --> 00:09:48,496
I just got a call from the owner.

113
00:09:48,496 --> 00:09:51,737
All roads leading into the mountain
have been closed since yesterday afternoon.

114
00:09:51,737 --> 00:09:54,805
And they've just imposed
an indefinite ban on entry.

115
00:09:54,805 --> 00:09:56,962
Looks like we're stranded.

116
00:10:28,045 --> 00:10:29,725
Where have you been?

117
00:10:29,725 --> 00:10:31,496
Put some clothes on and come out.

118
00:10:52,941 --> 00:10:56,196
So this is where they store
all the food supplies.

119
00:10:59,205 --> 00:11:00,837
But how did you find...

120
00:11:00,837 --> 00:11:02,662
I found out when I came to get some firewood.

121
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:07,457
Let's take the things that'll spoil quickly
or can't be eaten once frozen.

122
00:11:07,457 --> 00:11:09,162
Oh, okay.

123
00:11:10,649 --> 00:11:12,657
There isn't much left here either.

124
00:11:12,657 --> 00:11:13,804
Still, if we ration it,

125
00:11:13,804 --> 00:11:15,713
the two of us should
be able to make it for about a week, right?

126
00:11:15,713 --> 00:11:17,785
The roads will be open by then, right?

127
00:11:17,785 --> 00:11:19,729
It could take longer.

128
00:11:27,225 --> 00:11:28,945
Oh, oh!

129
00:11:28,945 --> 00:11:30,081
It's okay.

130
00:11:30,081 --> 00:11:33,229
Oh, this is for hunting.
That startled you, right?

131
00:11:33,229 --> 00:11:37,417
Lodges this deep in the mountains
usually keep one of these around.

132
00:11:37,417 --> 00:11:39,262
Because of wild animals.

133
00:11:43,501 --> 00:11:45,829
Oh, don't touch that carelessly...

134
00:11:47,241 --> 00:11:48,941
It's dangerous.

135
00:12:05,237 --> 00:12:07,321
Wait, those are bullets?

136
00:12:07,321 --> 00:12:09,264
That's...

137
00:12:09,264 --> 00:12:11,662
Why are you taking those...

138
00:12:15,185 --> 00:12:18,196
Huh? Why are you... Why are you taking them?

139
00:12:29,985 --> 00:12:33,797
Is there anything making
you uncomfortable here...

140
00:12:33,797 --> 00:12:35,109
Like what?

141
00:12:35,109 --> 00:12:38,149
I mean, since it's just the two of us here,

142
00:12:38,149 --> 00:12:41,549
you might feel a little uneasy as a woman.

143
00:12:41,549 --> 00:12:43,249
Not really.

144
00:12:44,753 --> 00:12:46,453
That's a relief.

145
00:12:48,761 --> 00:12:50,829
What's your name?

146
00:12:51,709 --> 00:12:54,821
Oh, I'm Kwon Tae Seong, Kwon Tae Seong.

147
00:12:54,821 --> 00:12:58,996
If you're uncomfortable, you can just
give me a fake name or a nickname.

148
00:12:58,996 --> 00:13:01,961
I just need something to call you.

149
00:13:01,961 --> 00:13:04,796
It's Bo Na, Yoo Bo Na.

150
00:13:05,513 --> 00:13:07,365
Oh, Yoo Bo Na?

151
00:13:07,365 --> 00:13:09,065
Yoo...

152
00:13:19,521 --> 00:13:22,841
The pipes aren't going to freeze, are they?

153
00:13:22,841 --> 00:13:25,162
We can just leave the water running a little.

154
00:13:27,693 --> 00:13:31,733
Or the roof collapsing...
from all the snow...

155
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:33,862
It won't collapse from this much snow.

156
00:13:36,825 --> 00:13:38,629
The gas could get cut off too.

157
00:13:38,629 --> 00:13:40,073
There's a portable stove in the shed.

158
00:13:40,073 --> 00:13:41,773
I see.

159
00:13:43,173 --> 00:13:45,905
What should we make for dinner?

160
00:13:45,905 --> 00:13:49,396
Do you happen to know how to cook?

161
00:14:11,265 --> 00:14:13,697
We should add some soybean paste, right?

162
00:14:13,697 --> 00:14:15,733
I suppose so.

163
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:17,996
But how much...

164
00:14:18,609 --> 00:14:20,309
Is that too little?

165
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:24,553
[For stock]
We should add some anchovies, right?

166
00:14:24,553 --> 00:14:26,253
I guess so.

167
00:14:27,189 --> 00:14:28,217
Two?

168
00:14:28,217 --> 00:14:29,509
Two?

169
00:14:29,509 --> 00:14:31,177
- Two?
- Isn't that too many?

170
00:14:31,177 --> 00:14:33,129
At least one each...

171
00:14:34,905 --> 00:14:36,605
Yeah.

172
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:49,169
What's the problem...

173
00:15:33,013 --> 00:15:34,501
You go ahead.

174
00:15:34,501 --> 00:15:36,496
No, you go ahead first...

175
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,033
Good night.

176
00:17:05,437 --> 00:17:09,649
I'm not usually the type
to get scared easily.

177
00:17:09,649 --> 00:17:11,877
But I've never experienced

178
00:17:11,877 --> 00:17:16,429
a snowstorm this severe,
with such strong winds, in my life.

179
00:17:19,537 --> 00:17:22,841
The power's out, the boiler's down,

180
00:17:22,841 --> 00:17:25,096
there's no phone service,

181
00:17:26,661 --> 00:17:29,073
and we're running out of food...

182
00:17:29,073 --> 00:17:31,762
We're basically refugees, aren't we?

183
00:17:36,169 --> 00:17:39,157
And the snow just keeps coming down.

184
00:17:39,157 --> 00:17:41,429
It'll stop tomorrow.

185
00:17:44,289 --> 00:17:46,129
How do you know that...

186
00:17:57,896 --> 00:18:00,629
Then I'll head back to my room.

187
00:18:00,629 --> 00:18:02,762
Sleep here with me.

188
00:18:04,577 --> 00:18:07,889
You'll freeze to death
sleeping alone in that room.

189
00:18:07,889 --> 00:18:10,662
This is the warmest spot, anyway.

190
00:18:25,389 --> 00:18:27,994
What's the first thing you want to do

191
00:18:27,994 --> 00:18:30,562
when you leave the mountain, Ms. Yoo Bo Na?

192
00:18:33,329 --> 00:18:37,897
I mean, once you go back to your normal life?

193
00:18:37,897 --> 00:18:40,037
Well... nothing, really.

194
00:18:40,037 --> 00:18:41,462
There's nothing you want to do?

195
00:18:41,462 --> 00:18:44,297
Or anyone you want to see?

196
00:18:44,297 --> 00:18:46,562
No, nothing.

197
00:18:48,309 --> 00:18:49,658
<i>Huh?</i>

198
00:18:49,658 --> 00:18:52,462
I came here
because I don't want to do anything.

199
00:18:52,462 --> 00:18:54,396
<i>I just want some peace and quiet.</i>

200
00:19:42,101 --> 00:19:45,165
<i>♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪</i>

201
00:19:45,165 --> 00:19:47,885
<i>♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪</i>

202
00:19:47,885 --> 00:19:50,909
<i>♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪</i>

203
00:19:50,909 --> 00:19:54,496
<i>♪ And a happy New Year ♪</i>

204
00:19:55,225 --> 00:19:58,065
Well, our situation may not be ideal,

205
00:19:58,065 --> 00:20:01,957
but just like you predicted,
the snow has stopped.

206
00:20:01,957 --> 00:20:04,677
And it's Christmas today.

207
00:20:04,677 --> 00:20:06,662
Merry Christmas!

208
00:20:07,313 --> 00:20:09,013
You didn't know, right?

209
00:20:10,737 --> 00:20:16,462
Oh, this is a Christmas present
for you, Bo Na!

210
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:42,629
Bo Na... Bo Na.

211
00:20:43,249 --> 00:20:47,862
Do you see that little bird
peeking out between the branches?

212
00:20:48,893 --> 00:20:51,462
That wouldn't even be a single bite.

213
00:20:56,269 --> 00:20:59,377
Isn't it tiny and adorable?
So cute and round?

214
00:20:59,377 --> 00:21:03,209
Oh, it's incredible how it survives
so bravely in weather this cold.

215
00:21:03,209 --> 00:21:04,996
Pretty amazing, huh?

216
00:21:23,397 --> 00:21:25,457
Bo Na.

217
00:21:25,457 --> 00:21:28,129
Come over here and look.

218
00:21:29,645 --> 00:21:33,073
What do you think of
when you see icicles, Bo Na?

219
00:21:33,073 --> 00:21:36,196
It'd be perfect for piercing
a vital spot in one go.

220
00:21:41,725 --> 00:21:44,329
Aren't they beautiful and crystal clear?

221
00:21:45,297 --> 00:21:48,689
When I was little, I used to suck on them.

222
00:21:48,689 --> 00:21:51,329
We could make shaved ice with them, right?

223
00:22:01,073 --> 00:22:02,773
Bo Na!

224
00:22:04,217 --> 00:22:06,153
Ta-da!

225
00:22:06,153 --> 00:22:08,557
I found this stuck in the firewood.

226
00:22:08,557 --> 00:22:10,337
Isn't it incredibly romantic?

227
00:22:10,337 --> 00:22:13,762
It was around this time of year
when I first met you.

228
00:22:16,899 --> 00:22:19,129
Can you hold out your hand for a second?

229
00:22:29,781 --> 00:22:31,996
I'll see if I can find another one.

230
00:22:45,473 --> 00:22:47,929
I think the sweet potatoes are almost done.

231
00:22:53,405 --> 00:22:55,396
It's so atmospheric, isn't it?

232
00:23:02,557 --> 00:23:05,196
It would've been nice to have some meat too.

233
00:23:10,629 --> 00:23:13,937
I actually came here to report a story once.

234
00:23:13,937 --> 00:23:16,362
Oh, I'm a reporter.

235
00:23:19,837 --> 00:23:21,537
Anyway,

236
00:23:23,101 --> 00:23:25,877
I parked my car down the mountain
and started walking up.

237
00:23:25,877 --> 00:23:27,052
I must've taken a wrong turn,

238
00:23:27,052 --> 00:23:30,462
and no matter how far I walked,
I couldn't find my way.

239
00:23:30,462 --> 00:23:32,981
I was hungry. My legs were aching.

240
00:23:32,981 --> 00:23:36,741
I thought, "I can't go any farther,"
and just sat down.

241
00:23:36,741 --> 00:23:42,657
But then, I casually turned my head,
and right in front of me,

242
00:23:42,657 --> 00:23:46,429
there was a field of wildflowers.

243
00:23:46,429 --> 00:23:47,721
Like some hidden paradise,

244
00:23:47,721 --> 00:23:52,681
a huge field of flowers spread out
in a place I'd never have expected.

245
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:55,913
That was the first time
I'd ever felt my heart drop

246
00:23:55,913 --> 00:23:58,705
at the sight of something so beautiful.

247
00:23:58,705 --> 00:24:00,929
As I gazed quietly at the field of flowers,

248
00:24:00,929 --> 00:24:04,429
my heart grew more generous,
and my mood lifted.

249
00:24:05,421 --> 00:24:09,045
Like every cell in my body
was coming back to life, you know?

250
00:24:09,045 --> 00:24:13,181
Thanks to that, I was able to get
my energy back and start moving again.

251
00:24:13,181 --> 00:24:16,462
Oh, and of course, I finished
my reporting without a hitch.

252
00:24:17,253 --> 00:24:19,382
I think that's the power of a beautiful view.

253
00:24:19,382 --> 00:24:21,993
My own little views that give me energy

254
00:24:21,993 --> 00:24:26,805
when I'm tired and help me
get moving again when I stop.

255
00:24:26,805 --> 00:24:30,217
For some people, it could be something

256
00:24:30,217 --> 00:24:36,273
as ordinary as flowers, sunsets,
or stars in the night sky.

257
00:24:36,273 --> 00:24:40,162
For someone else,
it might be a particular moment.

258
00:24:42,041 --> 00:24:44,629
Or even a person.

259
00:24:47,325 --> 00:24:51,096
Have you ever had a beautiful moment
like that in your life, Bo Na?

260
00:24:55,101 --> 00:24:57,241
No.

261
00:24:57,241 --> 00:24:59,062
You haven't? Not even once?

262
00:24:59,062 --> 00:25:02,562
Because I've never thought of
anything as beautiful.

263
00:25:06,496 --> 00:25:08,929
From now on, I'll show you plenty.

264
00:25:14,329 --> 00:25:15,853
I mean...

265
00:25:15,853 --> 00:25:21,129
It's nighttime here
and too dark to see anything pretty.

266
00:25:29,621 --> 00:25:32,029
But there is one beautiful sight.

267
00:25:50,253 --> 00:25:52,796
Oh, the sweet potatoes are going to burn.

268
00:26:14,205 --> 00:26:15,929
Your face is getting burnt.

269
00:27:03,641 --> 00:27:05,341
Why is the gun...

270
00:27:11,417 --> 00:27:13,117
Ms. Yoo Bo Na!

271
00:27:20,797 --> 00:27:22,497
Bo Na!

272
00:27:25,649 --> 00:27:27,349
Bo Na!

273
00:27:35,185 --> 00:27:37,596
Bo Na! Where are you?

274
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:52,896
Bo Na!

275
00:27:53,965 --> 00:27:56,017
Bo Na!

276
00:27:56,017 --> 00:27:57,929
Bo Na!

277
00:28:01,049 --> 00:28:02,929
Bo Na!

278
00:28:04,797 --> 00:28:06,918
Bo Na!

279
00:28:06,918 --> 00:28:08,796
Bo Na!

280
00:28:16,165 --> 00:28:17,865
Bo Na!

281
00:28:19,534 --> 00:28:21,262
Bo Na!

282
00:29:04,697 --> 00:29:07,429
Why is he lying here like this...

283
00:29:11,637 --> 00:29:13,929
I can't even call an ambulance in this place.

284
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:42,613
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

285
00:29:44,861 --> 00:29:47,481
<i>As time passed, I became a reporter.</i>

286
00:29:47,481 --> 00:29:49,181
[Spring, 2017]
Mr. Oh!

287
00:29:49,181 --> 00:29:52,029
Do you admit to stock manipulation,
embezzlement, and breach of trust?

288
00:29:52,029 --> 00:29:54,093
There are hundreds of victims!

289
00:29:54,093 --> 00:29:55,329
Don't you feel sorry?

290
00:29:55,329 --> 00:30:00,657
<i>I've watched countless offenders
escape proper punishment.</i>

291
00:30:00,657 --> 00:30:01,825
Mr. Oh!

292
00:30:01,825 --> 00:30:03,996
<i>I've spent countless days feeling despair</i>

293
00:30:03,996 --> 00:30:05,956
<i>as I faced the walls in our society that</i>

294
00:30:05,956 --> 00:30:07,296
<i>no amount of effort
seemed able to break through.</i>

295
00:30:07,296 --> 00:30:08,613
[Kingfisher's Target: A Child Sex Abuser]
<i>The gunman known as Kingfisher</i>

296
00:30:08,613 --> 00:30:09,613
<i>has committed another murder...</i>

297
00:30:09,613 --> 00:30:10,719
<i>But even during that time,</i>

298
00:30:10,719 --> 00:30:12,933
[Kingfisher Victim Exposed For]
<i>Kingfisher continued his work.</i>

299
00:30:12,933 --> 00:30:15,662
[Exploiting Disabled Workers]
<i>Many people tried to figure out who he was</i>

300
00:30:15,662 --> 00:30:17,929
[A Week Later, Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>and speculated on why he did such things.</i>

301
00:30:17,929 --> 00:30:19,061
[Victim Was a Gangster]
<i>But I didn't.</i>

302
00:30:19,061 --> 00:30:20,657
<i>Was found shot.</i>

303
00:30:20,657 --> 00:30:23,802
<i>- I never carelessly speculated about him.
- The weight is on the fact</i>

304
00:30:23,802 --> 00:30:25,762
[Rental Scam Real Estate CEO Found Shot Dead]
<i>that it was Kingfisher's crime.</i>

305
00:30:27,141 --> 00:30:30,117
<i>So even if Kingfisher's identity
is revealed someday,</i>

306
00:30:30,117 --> 00:30:32,289
<i>I won't be surprised.</i>

307
00:30:32,289 --> 00:30:34,662
<i>Even if he's someone
who defies all expectations,</i>

308
00:30:34,662 --> 00:30:37,445
<i>like a white-haired old man,</i>

309
00:30:37,445 --> 00:30:41,569
<i>I'll simply look forward to the day
I finally meet him.</i>

310
00:30:41,569 --> 00:30:45,077
<i>I want to sit beside him by the campfire</i>

311
00:30:45,077 --> 00:30:48,113
<i>and listen to him talk about
his life all night.</i>

312
00:30:48,113 --> 00:30:51,141
<i>Like two strangers who met while traveling,</i>

313
00:30:51,141 --> 00:30:54,529
<i>or old friends seeing each other again
after a long time.</i>

314
00:30:55,453 --> 00:30:59,313
<i>Without asking anything,
I could simply listen,</i>

315
00:30:59,313 --> 00:31:04,096
<i>with a warm cup of coffee or tea by my side.</i>

316
00:31:44,309 --> 00:31:46,296
You're awake?

317
00:31:57,353 --> 00:31:59,569
I was so scared.

318
00:31:59,569 --> 00:32:01,729
I was afraid you might disappear.

319
00:32:02,389 --> 00:32:05,496
I'm so relieved, really relieved,
that you came back safe.

320
00:32:13,605 --> 00:32:15,996
Thank you for coming back.

321
00:32:52,605 --> 00:32:55,062
What's this? Where did you get the meat...

322
00:32:55,773 --> 00:32:58,221
I found some in the freezer.

323
00:32:58,221 --> 00:33:01,529
Was there chicken? How did I not see it?

324
00:33:05,357 --> 00:33:07,057
Thank you for the meal.

325
00:33:27,945 --> 00:33:30,097
This is so good.

326
00:33:30,097 --> 00:33:33,762
I think this is the best chicken porridge
I've ever had.

327
00:33:38,021 --> 00:33:40,829
But do you always cry that easily?

328
00:33:44,777 --> 00:33:46,477
Pardon?

329
00:33:49,441 --> 00:33:51,141
No, I don't.

330
00:33:55,929 --> 00:33:59,096
It's actually the first time I've cried
since I graduated from elementary school.

331
00:34:07,197 --> 00:34:09,062
It's a first for me too.

332
00:34:10,729 --> 00:34:12,849
What is?

333
00:34:12,849 --> 00:34:15,662
Someone crying because
they were afraid I'd disappear.

334
00:34:17,545 --> 00:34:20,196
I didn't come here to die.

335
00:34:21,513 --> 00:34:24,229
I've never even thought about wanting to die.

336
00:34:28,281 --> 00:34:31,262
I really... I didn't know you thought that.

337
00:34:31,949 --> 00:34:33,005
Then what about the gun?

338
00:34:33,005 --> 00:34:35,729
I just put it back where it was.

339
00:34:39,589 --> 00:34:41,662
Then what about the gunshot?

340
00:34:43,149 --> 00:34:45,996
It seems like there might be a hunter around.

341
00:34:46,781 --> 00:34:50,865
Right, how did I get here...

342
00:34:50,865 --> 00:34:54,065
Did you carry me here on your back...

343
00:34:54,065 --> 00:34:56,362
I rolled you here.

344
00:34:58,829 --> 00:35:00,529
What?

345
00:35:01,785 --> 00:35:04,196
We're out of water. I'll get you some water.

346
00:35:14,089 --> 00:35:15,884
[Seasoned Salt]

347
00:35:52,773 --> 00:35:54,996
Bo Na, here!

348
00:35:59,637 --> 00:36:02,962
This is the wildflower field
I told you about.

349
00:36:05,613 --> 00:36:09,529
It's my first time seeing the landscape
look like this when it snows too.

350
00:36:12,929 --> 00:36:15,001
I wish there had been flowers here.

351
00:36:15,001 --> 00:36:16,701
But it's winter,

352
00:36:17,797 --> 00:36:19,862
and snow flowers are flowers too.

353
00:36:40,425 --> 00:36:42,662
I like you, Bo Na.

354
00:36:50,113 --> 00:36:52,629
You don't really know much about me, do you?

355
00:36:52,629 --> 00:36:55,529
You're right. I don't know much about you.

356
00:36:56,165 --> 00:36:58,196
I know your name, but...

357
00:36:59,373 --> 00:37:01,396
I don't even know if it's your real name.

358
00:37:01,396 --> 00:37:04,262
I don't know where you were born,
how you grew up,

359
00:37:05,253 --> 00:37:08,949
what your family is like,
or what you do for a living.

360
00:37:08,949 --> 00:37:13,696
I don't know why you were
standing there that day

361
00:37:14,633 --> 00:37:16,469
when we first met.

362
00:37:16,469 --> 00:37:19,096
But I do know some sides of you, Bo Na.

363
00:37:19,096 --> 00:37:21,229
You climb rough mountain paths
without hesitation.

364
00:37:21,229 --> 00:37:23,793
You prefer meat over vegetables.

365
00:37:23,793 --> 00:37:28,437
And in a crisis, you're calmer
and stronger than anyone.

366
00:37:28,437 --> 00:37:30,137
And...

367
00:37:31,893 --> 00:37:36,293
you make the most delicious
chicken porridge in the world.

368
00:37:36,293 --> 00:37:38,289
Perhaps love begins

369
00:37:38,289 --> 00:37:40,369
when you find yourself drawn to

370
00:37:40,369 --> 00:37:43,862
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

371
00:37:45,769 --> 00:37:48,029
I've already fallen in love.

372
00:38:09,617 --> 00:38:12,396
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

373
00:38:13,573 --> 00:38:15,877
Please take care of me.

374
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:17,929
It's my first time with love.

375
00:38:40,417 --> 00:38:42,162
It's beautiful.

376
00:39:19,562 --> 00:39:24,105
My mom and my older sister
run a chicken shop together.

377
00:39:24,105 --> 00:39:26,185
Do you know what it is called?

378
00:39:26,185 --> 00:39:27,962
Tae Seong Chicken?

379
00:39:30,917 --> 00:39:36,013
My second oldest sister
works at an insurance company.

380
00:39:36,013 --> 00:39:37,913
And the youngest is Se Ah...

381
00:39:37,913 --> 00:39:43,596
So that woman on the rooftop was your sister.

382
00:39:44,773 --> 00:39:46,796
Oh, yes, that's right.

383
00:39:59,565 --> 00:40:02,509
Maybe it's because it's spring,
but you look healthier.

384
00:40:02,509 --> 00:40:04,729
Did you have a good vacation?

385
00:40:05,509 --> 00:40:07,209
Yes.

386
00:40:09,825 --> 00:40:13,529
Have you made up your mind?

387
00:40:22,705 --> 00:40:24,405
My resignation letter...

388
00:40:25,953 --> 00:40:28,001
Please throw it away.

389
00:40:28,001 --> 00:40:30,129
Please forget I ever submitted it.

390
00:40:37,017 --> 00:40:38,717
Alright.

391
00:40:40,761 --> 00:40:42,862
What made you come back?

392
00:40:49,073 --> 00:40:51,429
I saw a beautiful landscape.

393
00:40:52,157 --> 00:40:53,857
What?

394
00:40:59,029 --> 00:41:03,729
The ocean really is the best place
to clear your head, after all.

395
00:41:15,309 --> 00:41:17,557
- Hey, is it good?
- What do you want?

396
00:41:17,557 --> 00:41:19,701
- I asked if it's good.
- Go away.

397
00:41:19,701 --> 00:41:21,554
I said go away!

398
00:41:22,305 --> 00:41:25,365
Go away, hurry, go!

399
00:41:25,365 --> 00:41:27,537
Ma'am, ma'am!

400
00:41:27,537 --> 00:41:28,921
I'll push it for you.

401
00:41:28,921 --> 00:41:30,856
- Huh?
- Who are you?

402
00:41:42,353 --> 00:41:44,800
[Not Today]

403
00:41:44,824 --> 00:41:45,993
[Social Affairs Desk]

404
00:41:45,993 --> 00:41:48,109
Hey.

405
00:41:48,109 --> 00:41:50,169
- Why are you wearing a suit?
- I don't know, man.

406
00:41:50,169 --> 00:41:51,869
You came early?

407
00:42:04,105 --> 00:42:05,501
What's this?

408
00:42:05,501 --> 00:42:10,956
It's to thank you for giving me the chance
to prove myself with my reporting.

409
00:42:12,677 --> 00:42:15,122
Thank you. I'll enjoy it.

410
00:42:16,217 --> 00:42:18,997
I'm about to be completely broke.

411
00:42:18,997 --> 00:42:20,697
Why?

412
00:42:23,105 --> 00:42:24,105
Thank you!

413
00:42:24,105 --> 00:42:25,805
Oh, jeez.

414
00:42:28,469 --> 00:42:29,637
Seriously...

415
00:42:29,637 --> 00:42:33,373
I've also decided to buy
a huge team dinner soon!

416
00:42:33,373 --> 00:42:36,689
A round of applause for our Hae Na!

417
00:42:45,481 --> 00:42:49,641
I made some egg rice this morning,
but I made way too much.

418
00:42:49,641 --> 00:42:51,721
I guess I tend to make too much.

419
00:42:51,721 --> 00:42:53,421
Here.

420
00:42:54,849 --> 00:42:56,733
Are you sure it's safe to eat?

421
00:42:56,733 --> 00:42:58,941
Don't eat it.

422
00:42:58,941 --> 00:43:00,689
I'll just eat it and die.

423
00:43:09,581 --> 00:43:11,889
Sometimes I can't believe it myself, either.

424
00:43:15,465 --> 00:43:18,853
I still can't believe I can cook like this.

425
00:43:18,853 --> 00:43:23,377
Jeez, you should've come to the housewarming.
There was a lot of good food.

426
00:43:23,377 --> 00:43:24,749
I'd just be a burden.

427
00:43:24,749 --> 00:43:26,349
Oh, dear.

428
00:43:26,349 --> 00:43:29,781
Hey, you seriously need to
cut down on instant food.

429
00:43:29,781 --> 00:43:31,585
You'll ruin your health.

430
00:43:31,585 --> 00:43:33,756
Is it good to have a family?

431
00:43:35,569 --> 00:43:36,841
Yeah, it's good.

432
00:43:36,841 --> 00:43:38,722
More than friends?

433
00:43:41,757 --> 00:43:43,589
Friends are...

434
00:43:44,549 --> 00:43:48,722
like guests who sometimes come to the island
where I live, bringing good food?

435
00:43:49,665 --> 00:43:51,389
Family is...

436
00:43:52,117 --> 00:43:55,665
the very island I'm standing on.

437
00:43:55,665 --> 00:43:59,156
My one and only island...

438
00:43:59,156 --> 00:44:02,022
in this endless sea, I guess?

439
00:44:02,956 --> 00:44:04,789
My little piece of land.

440
00:44:06,461 --> 00:44:09,165
You've got something
to protect now, Yoo Bo Na.

441
00:44:09,165 --> 00:44:11,025
You sound just like someone I know.

442
00:44:11,025 --> 00:44:12,725
Huh?

443
00:44:12,725 --> 00:44:14,656
That face of yours.

444
00:44:20,693 --> 00:44:22,233
Do you like it?

445
00:44:22,233 --> 00:44:24,277
It's made from a new lightweight material.

446
00:44:24,277 --> 00:44:26,256
Yeah, I like it.

447
00:44:29,001 --> 00:44:31,489
Can I borrow this for the weekend?

448
00:44:43,877 --> 00:44:46,673
If you're that curious,
why don't you go inside?

449
00:44:46,673 --> 00:44:48,973
What do you mean? I'm not curious.

450
00:44:48,973 --> 00:44:52,465
Those two are friends. They've known
each other since they were kids.

451
00:44:52,465 --> 00:44:57,122
Our brilliant Director Yoo,
and a filthy, smelly shut-in?

452
00:45:00,601 --> 00:45:02,137
What am I, by any chance?

453
00:45:02,137 --> 00:45:05,056
A sickly, obnoxious keyboard jockey.

454
00:45:05,056 --> 00:45:07,722
Jeez, I can't believe this.

455
00:45:13,009 --> 00:45:14,941
You forgot to take this.

456
00:45:14,941 --> 00:45:18,689
Se Ah put a lot of effort into making it.
Wouldn't it be rude not to take it?

457
00:45:24,273 --> 00:45:27,313
Man, a man really needs
to be good-looking, after all.

458
00:45:27,313 --> 00:45:30,661
So this is what they mean by
good looks getting you places.

459
00:45:30,661 --> 00:45:32,849
I know exactly how he feels.

460
00:45:32,849 --> 00:45:35,981
I was exactly like that when I was young.

461
00:45:35,981 --> 00:45:37,722
When?

462
00:45:38,422 --> 00:45:39,713
When I was young.

463
00:45:39,713 --> 00:45:42,722
That girl's got quite a taste...

464
00:45:46,881 --> 00:45:47,958
- It's good.
- Honey, I'll do it.

465
00:45:47,958 --> 00:45:49,093
You didn't even have lunch.

466
00:45:49,093 --> 00:45:51,001
- You need to eat more.
- I'm eating.

467
00:45:51,001 --> 00:45:52,237
- Eat the fish first.
- Okay, I will.

468
00:45:52,237 --> 00:45:53,913
Your favorite fish.

469
00:45:53,913 --> 00:45:55,397
Does your brother not have hands?

470
00:45:55,397 --> 00:45:58,589
The day you return my clothes,
let's go on a date.

471
00:46:07,605 --> 00:46:09,557
You crazy punk...

472
00:46:09,557 --> 00:46:11,956
Why did I even ask her that?

473
00:46:20,545 --> 00:46:22,309
What should I do?

474
00:46:27,121 --> 00:46:28,417
I don't have his number.

475
00:46:28,417 --> 00:46:29,809
Should I ask Bo Na?

476
00:46:29,809 --> 00:46:33,033
Then she'd probably tell me
to bring it to her office.

477
00:46:33,033 --> 00:46:37,056
Then what am I supposed to do about my date?

478
00:46:43,377 --> 00:46:46,589
Yes, Your Majesty. What is the matter?

479
00:46:47,737 --> 00:46:48,961
Jeez, Mom!

480
00:46:48,961 --> 00:46:51,156
I told you not to take orders
from that place.

481
00:46:51,156 --> 00:46:53,956
Why do you keep sending me
all the way over there...

482
00:46:56,373 --> 00:47:00,153
Mom, using highly skilled talent
like me for errands like this

483
00:47:00,153 --> 00:47:03,689
is a waste of national resources!

484
00:47:10,987 --> 00:47:13,532
[Tae Seong Chicken]

485
00:47:24,687 --> 00:47:26,641
[I'm here]

486
00:47:27,697 --> 00:47:29,685
Get off, get off!

487
00:47:29,685 --> 00:47:31,693
Darn it, I'm going!

488
00:47:31,693 --> 00:47:33,021
Let go!

489
00:47:33,021 --> 00:47:34,749
Darn it.

490
00:47:37,365 --> 00:47:39,109
Oh...

491
00:47:42,609 --> 00:47:45,856
The punk came in guilty,
and now he's laughing?

492
00:47:47,945 --> 00:47:50,529
Oh, Se Dol! You got here
sooner than I expected.

493
00:47:50,529 --> 00:47:52,337
Hey, you want to die?

494
00:47:52,337 --> 00:47:54,456
Don't you have a chicken shop
in your neighborhood?

495
00:47:54,456 --> 00:47:55,456
Yeah, we don't.

496
00:47:55,456 --> 00:47:57,174
This neighborhood's nothing but
pizza places and snack bars.

497
00:47:57,174 --> 00:47:59,457
Then eat pizza or snacks around here.

498
00:47:59,457 --> 00:48:01,689
Why are you boosting the sales of
a chicken shop in another neighborhood?

499
00:48:01,689 --> 00:48:03,789
Don't you have any respect
for the local economy?

500
00:48:03,789 --> 00:48:05,556
You brought plenty of
radish and salad, right?

501
00:48:05,556 --> 00:48:09,521
Keep ordering, and you might end up
getting fried with the chicken.

502
00:48:09,521 --> 00:48:10,673
Hey, just wear your helmet properly.

503
00:48:10,673 --> 00:48:12,397
Don't get slapped with a fine for no reason.

504
00:48:12,397 --> 00:48:13,589
I'm going.

505
00:48:13,589 --> 00:48:15,289
Go.

506
00:48:20,053 --> 00:48:22,021
What? I'm busy.

507
00:48:22,021 --> 00:48:25,933
From now on, answer my questions
short and sweet.

508
00:48:25,933 --> 00:48:27,193
Short and sweet about what?

509
00:48:27,193 --> 00:48:29,467
Say you're going on a first date
with some woman.

510
00:48:29,467 --> 00:48:30,753
- What?
- A first date.

511
00:48:30,753 --> 00:48:33,857
- With whom?
- Jeez, I'm just giving you an example.

512
00:48:33,857 --> 00:48:35,617
A hypothetical woman.

513
00:48:35,617 --> 00:48:38,053
- And?
- You ask her,

514
00:48:38,053 --> 00:48:40,489
"What would you like to do?"

515
00:48:41,233 --> 00:48:43,293
What do you mean? We have to eat.

516
00:48:43,293 --> 00:48:45,721
You jump straight to food
the second you meet?

517
00:48:45,721 --> 00:48:47,769
Then what do you do?

518
00:48:47,769 --> 00:48:49,149
Fine. Let's say you have a meal with her.

519
00:48:49,149 --> 00:48:53,513
Then if you say, "Let's get something
to eat first. What would you like?"

520
00:48:53,513 --> 00:48:56,099
What would she say that
you'd find attractive?

521
00:48:56,099 --> 00:48:58,822
Chicken feet! You love those.

522
00:49:00,077 --> 00:49:01,322
I do.

523
00:49:01,322 --> 00:49:06,145
But for a first date,
chicken feet might be a little...

524
00:49:06,145 --> 00:49:09,694
Then your second pick,
all-you-can-eat frozen pork belly?

525
00:49:09,694 --> 00:49:11,421
Jeez, forget the food.

526
00:49:11,421 --> 00:49:13,069
What about the hair?

527
00:49:13,069 --> 00:49:14,769
Bangs down?

528
00:49:16,433 --> 00:49:17,497
Or pushed back?

529
00:49:17,497 --> 00:49:19,813
Definitely bangs down.
You inevitably need to cover up a lot.

530
00:49:19,813 --> 00:49:22,622
Jeez, forget it. Just go eat your chicken.

531
00:49:22,622 --> 00:49:24,356
Jeez.

532
00:49:27,293 --> 00:49:29,222
This isn't about me, you know?

533
00:49:33,565 --> 00:49:35,265
What is she saying?

534
00:49:37,877 --> 00:49:39,577
Hold on.

535
00:49:42,997 --> 00:49:44,369
[If you keep thinking about someone all day,]

536
00:49:44,393 --> 00:49:46,681
[and smile every time they cross your mind,]
Wow, is this for real?

537
00:49:46,681 --> 00:49:49,656
[is that love?]
I'm the only guy around her.

538
00:49:49,656 --> 00:49:50,656
Could it be me?

539
00:49:50,656 --> 00:49:51,786
What do you mean, you?

540
00:49:51,786 --> 00:49:53,501
What? No, it's nothing.

541
00:49:53,501 --> 00:49:54,757
Come into the interrogation room.

542
00:49:54,757 --> 00:49:55,940
Why?

543
00:49:55,940 --> 00:49:56,973
It's about Hwang Cheol Beom.

544
00:49:56,973 --> 00:49:58,673
Now?

545
00:50:00,589 --> 00:50:02,501
Sir, please go ahead and eat this first.

546
00:50:02,501 --> 00:50:04,256
I'm heading to the interrogation room...

547
00:50:04,937 --> 00:50:06,125
Please don't eat my chicken.

548
00:50:06,125 --> 00:50:07,922
- Alright.
- Yeah.

549
00:50:09,696 --> 00:50:10,673
[Tae Seong Chicken]

550
00:50:11,305 --> 00:50:12,989
Ugh, Tae Seong Chicken again!

551
00:50:12,989 --> 00:50:14,089
"Why did you take so long?"

552
00:50:14,089 --> 00:50:16,156
"I reported this ages ago."

553
00:50:17,553 --> 00:50:19,422
"Why aren't you cuffing me already?"

554
00:50:21,585 --> 00:50:24,489
Apparently, he kept saying things like that.

555
00:50:25,585 --> 00:50:26,981
Mr. Hwang Cheol Beom,

556
00:50:26,981 --> 00:50:29,022
why did you do that
right after getting released?

557
00:50:29,022 --> 00:50:31,165
I don't know. Lost my temper?

558
00:50:31,165 --> 00:50:34,677
Oh, so you beat up random people
just because you were angry?

559
00:50:34,677 --> 00:50:38,489
Aggravated assault and bodily injury
will almost certainly get you prison time.

560
00:50:38,489 --> 00:50:42,961
And the sentence will be even harsher
when there are multiple random victims.

561
00:50:42,961 --> 00:50:46,309
Plus, with your prior violent offense,

562
00:50:46,309 --> 00:50:48,622
the repeat-offender enhancement
could keep you locked up for a long time.

563
00:50:48,622 --> 00:50:51,107
You just got out.
You really want to go back in already?

564
00:50:51,107 --> 00:50:52,741
Oh, it's fine.

565
00:50:52,741 --> 00:50:55,722
It's more comfortable in there than out here.

566
00:50:56,494 --> 00:50:59,705
Afraid you'll get shot if you go outside?

567
00:50:59,705 --> 00:51:03,381
You brutally killed your sister-in-law
when she resisted your attempted rape.

568
00:51:03,381 --> 00:51:04,781
You deserved life in prison,

569
00:51:04,781 --> 00:51:08,456
but you fed them that "sudden impulse"
and "mentally weak" nonsense

570
00:51:09,787 --> 00:51:11,989
and got just 15 years.

571
00:51:11,989 --> 00:51:13,793
You're exactly the kind of person
Kingfisher would target, aren't you?

572
00:51:13,793 --> 00:51:17,622
Yeah, I did that because I was afraid of
getting shot and dying. So what?

573
00:51:20,349 --> 00:51:23,753
Do you know what it's like
in prison right now?

574
00:51:23,753 --> 00:51:26,377
Everyone's anxious and making a fuss.

575
00:51:26,377 --> 00:51:28,529
Some guys who've done bad things
but got lighter sentences

576
00:51:28,529 --> 00:51:30,673
are causing trouble inside on purpose

577
00:51:30,673 --> 00:51:33,556
because they're afraid Kingfisher
will kill them once they're released.

578
00:51:33,556 --> 00:51:36,349
Better to stay inside
than to live in anxiety,

579
00:51:36,349 --> 00:51:39,456
shaking at the thought of bullets
flying from who knows where.

580
00:51:39,456 --> 00:51:42,993
Oh, a lot of the guys who got out before me

581
00:51:42,993 --> 00:51:44,902
have gone missing too.

582
00:51:44,902 --> 00:51:47,249
Are you saying some of them were shot dead?

583
00:51:47,249 --> 00:51:48,397
How would I know?

584
00:51:48,397 --> 00:51:50,356
Whether they died from getting shot,
or got hit by a car,

585
00:51:50,356 --> 00:51:52,797
or fell and died...

586
00:51:52,797 --> 00:51:55,794
And for all we know,
Kingfisher doesn't even always

587
00:51:55,794 --> 00:51:58,378
use a gun, right?

588
00:51:58,378 --> 00:52:03,322
Either way, everyone's saying
it's all Kingfisher's doing.

589
00:52:05,549 --> 00:52:10,756
And people can make mistakes in life, right?

590
00:52:10,756 --> 00:52:12,589
Hey, you punk.

591
00:52:13,640 --> 00:52:16,297
What you did wasn't a mistake.

592
00:52:16,297 --> 00:52:18,517
What?

593
00:52:18,517 --> 00:52:22,289
We spent taxpayers' money giving you
a chance to repent and rehabilitate,

594
00:52:22,289 --> 00:52:25,237
and this is what you do
the second you get out?

595
00:52:25,237 --> 00:52:26,613
And what about you people?

596
00:52:26,613 --> 00:52:29,356
Isn't all this happening because the police
can't catch Kingfisher?

597
00:52:29,356 --> 00:52:32,117
Is that why you only targeted
the elderly and women?

598
00:52:32,117 --> 00:52:34,754
Too scared to mess with younger men?

599
00:52:34,754 --> 00:52:37,361
You're just a pathetic coward
who can only prey on the weak!

600
00:52:37,361 --> 00:52:39,622
How dare you run your mouth!

601
00:52:42,321 --> 00:52:45,333
Jeez, he killed innocent people
and calls it a mistake?

602
00:52:45,333 --> 00:52:48,321
You being born is a mistake, you punk!

603
00:52:48,321 --> 00:52:50,206
Hey, Beom.

604
00:52:50,206 --> 00:52:51,948
Pick 20 recently released convicts

605
00:52:51,948 --> 00:52:54,429
who you think got light sentences
for the severity of their crimes,

606
00:52:54,429 --> 00:52:57,801
and find out what's happened to them
since they got out. Hurry.

607
00:52:57,801 --> 00:52:59,817
What? Why?

608
00:52:59,817 --> 00:53:01,281
Oh, you mean guys like him?

609
00:53:01,281 --> 00:53:03,144
Yes, understood.

610
00:53:03,144 --> 00:53:05,745
Did you look into that dead body
at the villa in Hyeonsa-dong?

611
00:53:05,745 --> 00:53:08,769
Oh, the guy who died with his face
in a bowl of jjajangmyeon?

612
00:53:08,769 --> 00:53:11,181
They didn't find anything in the autopsy.

613
00:53:11,181 --> 00:53:13,348
They checked his medical records
for any underlying condition,

614
00:53:13,348 --> 00:53:15,322
but they said there was nothing notable.

615
00:53:16,956 --> 00:53:17,956
Alright.

616
00:53:17,956 --> 00:53:19,099
Finish Hwang Cheol Beom's report

617
00:53:19,099 --> 00:53:21,197
and transfer the case
to the prosecution by tomorrow.

618
00:53:21,197 --> 00:53:22,785
I'm leaving.

619
00:53:22,785 --> 00:53:24,161
Where are you going?

620
00:53:24,161 --> 00:53:26,205
- The supermarket.
- What?

621
00:53:26,205 --> 00:53:28,069
The supermarket?

622
00:53:28,069 --> 00:53:32,456
Oh, boy, now I can finally sleep soundly.

623
00:53:37,722 --> 00:53:40,422
Oh, my legs.

624
00:53:42,769 --> 00:53:44,848
Good grief.

625
00:53:44,848 --> 00:53:51,022
All that scheming just to survive...

626
00:53:51,981 --> 00:53:55,813
But should prison

627
00:53:55,813 --> 00:53:59,625
be a hideout for criminals?

628
00:53:59,625 --> 00:54:04,922
We're already overcrowded as it is,
running out of space,

629
00:54:06,125 --> 00:54:07,977
aren't we?

630
00:54:07,977 --> 00:54:12,489
<i>♪ Dari-dari-da ♪</i>

631
00:54:58,745 --> 00:55:00,445
You're late.

632
00:55:01,693 --> 00:55:03,945
Why am I so bad at this
after not doing it for so long?

633
00:55:03,945 --> 00:55:07,277
How do you remember every year without fail?
Do you have an alarm set?

634
00:55:07,277 --> 00:55:09,289
Open the door. My legs hurt.

635
00:55:09,944 --> 00:55:11,621
Anyone would think you were the son.

636
00:55:11,621 --> 00:55:13,389
Then am I the daughter?
Did you get everything?

637
00:55:13,389 --> 00:55:15,189
I bought it all.

638
00:55:16,790 --> 00:55:20,060
[Lee Pil Ho, Ju Hye Gyeong]

639
00:55:38,422 --> 00:55:41,004
[Lee Pil Ho, Ju Hye Gyeong]

640
00:56:04,705 --> 00:56:06,913
It's almost been 20 years.

641
00:56:06,913 --> 00:56:10,256
Wow. Has it really been that long?

642
00:56:11,073 --> 00:56:14,221
Do you still dream about
what happened that day?

643
00:56:14,221 --> 00:56:17,261
Maybe it's because the ancestral rite
is coming up...

644
00:56:17,261 --> 00:56:19,056
I dreamed about it last night too.

645
00:56:25,241 --> 00:56:26,941
Have a drink.

646
00:56:31,729 --> 00:56:34,761
You talked me into becoming a reporter.

647
00:56:34,761 --> 00:56:36,781
And now that I think about it again,
it pisses me off.

648
00:56:36,781 --> 00:56:38,965
You bring that up every chance you get.

649
00:56:38,965 --> 00:56:41,065
Hey, do you think I wanted to?

650
00:56:41,065 --> 00:56:44,105
You made a huge fuss
about catching the culprit.

651
00:56:44,105 --> 00:56:45,745
And in the end, you couldn't catch him.

652
00:56:45,745 --> 00:56:48,401
Hey, but at least you became a cop, right?

653
00:56:48,401 --> 00:56:51,156
Oh, man, for real.

654
00:56:56,033 --> 00:56:58,041
Are the police in this country
really competent?

655
00:56:58,041 --> 00:57:02,389
If they're that competent, why did it
take them four years to catch him?

656
00:57:06,609 --> 00:57:10,033
That punk still hasn't been released, right?

657
00:57:10,033 --> 00:57:12,756
Not yet. Next year.

658
00:57:14,477 --> 00:57:16,261
Today...

659
00:57:16,261 --> 00:57:19,965
I saw a punk just like him.

660
00:57:19,965 --> 00:57:21,753
That punk said the same thing.

661
00:57:21,753 --> 00:57:24,865
That it wasn't intentional.
That it was a mistake.

662
00:57:24,865 --> 00:57:27,222
I wonder if he's still the same.

663
00:57:27,222 --> 00:57:30,956
No remorse, no rehabilitation.

664
00:57:32,949 --> 00:57:35,189
Has he changed at all?

665
00:57:37,461 --> 00:57:39,121
Pretty. Are these hyacinths?

666
00:57:39,145 --> 00:57:41,605
Yeah, that's right.

667
00:57:43,325 --> 00:57:44,337
Ma'am!

668
00:57:44,337 --> 00:57:46,838
- Yeah.
- I've finished picking out the flowers.

669
00:57:46,838 --> 00:57:48,337
Oh, they're lovely!

670
00:57:48,337 --> 00:57:51,645
Who did our Yul pick such pretty flowers for?

671
00:57:51,645 --> 00:57:54,045
- It's a secret!
- Huh? My goodness.

672
00:57:54,045 --> 00:57:55,905
She's all grown up now,
knowing about secrets.

673
00:57:55,905 --> 00:57:57,761
It feels like just yesterday
she could barely say a word.

674
00:57:57,761 --> 00:58:00,941
Now she often tries to outsmart me.
I can't handle her.

675
00:58:00,941 --> 00:58:02,341
Oh, dear.

676
00:58:02,341 --> 00:58:05,313
Well, even the mighty Yoo Bo Na
has someone she can't beat.

677
00:58:05,313 --> 00:58:08,917
Well, that's what kids are like.

678
00:58:08,917 --> 00:58:11,701
I don't know if I'm doing a good job.

679
00:58:11,701 --> 00:58:13,313
What do you mean?

680
00:58:13,313 --> 00:58:18,138
The fact that you're worrying about that
is proof you're doing a good job.

681
00:58:19,257 --> 00:58:21,229
Now that I think about it, Yoo Bo Na,

682
00:58:21,229 --> 00:58:24,005
it reminds me of when you first had Yul.

683
00:58:25,453 --> 00:58:27,772
And the things you said back then too.

684
00:58:30,841 --> 00:58:32,205
Yul, no! Don't do that!

685
00:58:32,205 --> 00:58:34,117
Oh, dear, Yul, Yul!

686
00:58:34,117 --> 00:58:36,681
No, don't.

687
00:58:36,681 --> 00:58:40,038
Ma'am, what's the room over there?

688
00:58:41,005 --> 00:58:43,872
That's my secret too.

689
00:58:46,673 --> 00:58:48,638
Tell me the truth.

690
00:58:49,381 --> 00:58:51,472
You're a member...

691
00:58:52,961 --> 00:58:54,861
of the Kingfisher fan club, aren't you?

692
00:58:54,861 --> 00:58:57,373
What are you talking about, you crazy punk?

693
00:58:57,373 --> 00:59:03,025
You were obsessed with digging
into Kingfisher until a few years ago.

694
00:59:03,025 --> 00:59:04,857
You were constantly hounding me about it.

695
00:59:04,857 --> 00:59:08,269
Then one day, you just stopped.

696
00:59:08,269 --> 00:59:10,101
Why? Why all of a sudden? Why?

697
00:59:10,101 --> 00:59:11,965
Come on, be honest with me. What? Why?

698
00:59:11,965 --> 00:59:15,089
You're a Kingfisher fan, aren't you?

699
00:59:15,089 --> 00:59:16,652
Hey, enough nonsense.

700
00:59:16,652 --> 00:59:19,349
There's something
I've honestly wondered about for a long time.

701
00:59:19,349 --> 00:59:23,872
Why are you so obsessed with
catching Kingfisher?

702
00:59:25,201 --> 00:59:28,137
You punk, you must be the Kingfisher fan...

703
00:59:28,137 --> 00:59:30,238
Fan club president, right?

704
00:59:30,238 --> 00:59:32,213
- Hey, hey!
- King...

705
00:59:32,213 --> 00:59:36,017
I'm a cop!

706
00:59:36,017 --> 00:59:39,277
Yeah, you're a cop. So what?

707
00:59:39,277 --> 00:59:41,701
You're the family of a crime victim.

708
00:59:41,701 --> 00:59:43,561
I know. I know that too.

709
00:59:43,561 --> 00:59:46,025
Oh, Kingfisher?

710
00:59:46,025 --> 00:59:47,185
He's cool.

711
00:59:47,185 --> 00:59:50,133
Like some hero who takes down evil.

712
00:59:50,133 --> 00:59:54,037
Like a grim reaper taking revenge for me.

713
00:59:54,037 --> 00:59:57,549
But there's a side of him people don't know.

714
00:59:57,549 --> 01:00:01,238
A punk who shot a dad dead

715
01:00:02,597 --> 01:00:06,053
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

716
01:00:06,053 --> 01:00:09,417
Four years ago, at the scene of
Kingfisher's last known crime.

717
01:00:09,417 --> 01:00:14,697
The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.

718
01:00:14,697 --> 01:00:16,405
Jeez.

719
01:00:16,405 --> 01:00:17,765
Hey.

720
01:00:17,765 --> 01:00:22,873
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

721
01:00:22,873 --> 01:00:27,305
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

722
01:00:28,825 --> 01:00:30,075
<i>No matter what anyone says,</i>

723
01:00:30,075 --> 01:00:31,441
- <i>to me, Kingfisher is...</i>
- Yul, is it pretty?

724
01:00:31,441 --> 01:00:33,097
Yeah!

725
01:00:33,097 --> 01:00:39,305
<i>a cold-blooded,
heartless psychopath and murderer.</i>

726
01:00:39,305 --> 01:00:41,472
I feel like I'm going to throw up.

727
01:00:42,465 --> 01:00:45,438
- Huh?
- I seriously feel like throwing up.

728
01:00:48,338 --> 01:00:50,672
Aim properly!

729
01:00:52,785 --> 01:00:55,538
Otherwise, I'll have to clean it up.

730
01:00:56,685 --> 01:01:00,805
If he were just a psychopath
who killed anyone,

731
01:01:00,805 --> 01:01:04,772
it'd be easier to call him pure evil.

732
01:01:05,972 --> 01:01:12,849
But that punk only kills criminals,

733
01:01:12,849 --> 01:01:17,873
so people can't decide
whether he's good or evil.

734
01:01:17,873 --> 01:01:23,161
He taps into the dark side

735
01:01:23,161 --> 01:01:27,337
hidden deep inside everyone.

736
01:01:27,337 --> 01:01:29,572
What a bad punk!

737
01:01:36,957 --> 01:01:38,753
I have something to confess.

738
01:01:38,753 --> 01:01:40,905
You want to die?

739
01:01:41,825 --> 01:01:43,377
Get your hands off me.

740
01:01:43,377 --> 01:01:45,077
I...

741
01:01:47,541 --> 01:01:49,305
I know.

742
01:01:50,105 --> 01:01:53,505
I have a gun at the station, you know?

743
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,465
I... know who Kingfisher is.

744
01:02:00,465 --> 01:02:02,165
What?

745
01:02:18,273 --> 01:02:20,005
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong.

746
01:02:20,613 --> 01:02:25,297
Forget everything that happened today.

747
01:02:25,297 --> 01:02:30,338
And from now on, you'd better
stop looking into Kingfisher.

748
01:02:34,605 --> 01:02:37,038
If you break your promise...

749
01:02:58,525 --> 01:03:00,509
Honey, why are you up so early?

750
01:03:00,509 --> 01:03:02,238
Huh? Well...

751
01:03:02,238 --> 01:03:03,373
Daddy!

752
01:03:03,373 --> 01:03:05,401
Oh, Yul!

753
01:03:05,401 --> 01:03:08,001
Were you playing with Kkongsoon?

754
01:03:08,001 --> 01:03:09,765
Oh, Daddy, you smell like alcohol.

755
01:03:09,765 --> 01:03:10,981
Oh, put me down.

756
01:03:10,981 --> 01:03:12,293
I'm sorry.

757
01:03:12,293 --> 01:03:14,805
I'll brush my teeth and hug you later.

758
01:03:18,565 --> 01:03:21,393
How much did you drink
with Dong Jin last night?

759
01:03:21,393 --> 01:03:22,941
Ugh, I don't know.

760
01:03:22,941 --> 01:03:26,261
He suddenly went on a drinking binge.
What time did I get home last night?

761
01:03:26,261 --> 01:03:27,693
Around 2 AM?

762
01:03:27,693 --> 01:03:31,313
You came home in a taxi, showered,
changed, and went straight to bed.

763
01:03:31,313 --> 01:03:32,961
And you don't remember any of it?

764
01:03:32,961 --> 01:03:34,709
Wow. I must've completely blacked out.

765
01:03:34,709 --> 01:03:36,249
I don't remember any of it.

766
01:03:36,249 --> 01:03:37,813
- Really?
- Yeah.

767
01:03:37,813 --> 01:03:38,937
Really?

768
01:03:38,937 --> 01:03:40,429
Are you going somewhere?

769
01:03:40,429 --> 01:03:43,013
Yeah, I have something
to take care of real quick.

770
01:03:43,013 --> 01:03:45,413
Yul, come eat. Hurry.

771
01:03:45,413 --> 01:03:47,669
It's the weekend.

772
01:03:47,669 --> 01:03:49,409
I'll be back soon.

773
01:03:49,409 --> 01:03:52,225
You can look after Yul while I'm gone, right?

774
01:03:52,225 --> 01:03:53,225
Of course.

775
01:03:53,225 --> 01:03:56,333
I'm still pretty hungover,
but I can handle it.

776
01:03:56,333 --> 01:03:59,057
Honey, you really reek of alcohol.
Go brush your teeth. Hurry.

777
01:03:59,057 --> 01:04:00,577
Sorry.

778
01:04:00,577 --> 01:04:02,681
Yul!

779
01:04:02,681 --> 01:04:04,669
Yul!

780
01:04:04,669 --> 01:04:06,641
That's right.

781
01:04:06,641 --> 01:04:08,838
All right, pick up your spoon.

782
01:04:36,449 --> 01:04:38,165
<i>Hi, Bo Na.</i>

783
01:04:38,165 --> 01:04:40,577
<i>Are your Achilles' heels doing well?</i>

784
01:04:40,577 --> 01:04:41,817
<i>I miss you.</i>

785
01:04:41,817 --> 01:04:43,593
<i>I'll come to you.</i>

786
01:04:43,593 --> 01:04:49,001
<i>I hope I finally get to meet them this time.</i>

787
01:04:49,001 --> 01:04:50,705
<i>From your friend.</i>

788
01:04:54,141 --> 01:04:57,872
I'm sure I talked about
something important...

789
01:05:00,173 --> 01:05:04,672
Daddy, why did you color the rainbow black?

790
01:05:05,285 --> 01:05:08,041
Oh, sorry.

791
01:05:08,041 --> 01:05:09,889
Stop!

792
01:05:09,889 --> 01:05:12,138
<i>I have something to confess.</i>

793
01:05:12,138 --> 01:05:14,505
Actually, I...

794
01:05:14,505 --> 01:05:16,205
I know.

795
01:05:17,397 --> 01:05:19,605
I know...

796
01:05:19,605 --> 01:05:22,072
who Kingfisher is.

797
01:05:43,401 --> 01:05:46,381
<i>Hey, what?</i>

798
01:05:46,381 --> 01:05:49,069
Go home and sleep.

799
01:05:49,069 --> 01:05:51,501
I saw him. I really did.

800
01:05:51,501 --> 01:05:53,765
Saw what? Who?

801
01:05:53,765 --> 01:05:56,545
Kingfisher!

802
01:05:56,545 --> 01:05:58,189
Kingfisher!

803
01:05:58,189 --> 01:05:59,353
Kingfisher?

804
01:05:59,353 --> 01:06:00,541
Yeah!

805
01:06:00,541 --> 01:06:02,338
Really?

806
01:06:02,338 --> 01:06:04,069
Lucky you.

807
01:06:04,069 --> 01:06:07,369
Hey, what does he look like?

808
01:06:07,369 --> 01:06:09,069
Kingfisher?

809
01:06:17,261 --> 01:06:19,648
[Seul Gi]

810
01:06:25,869 --> 01:06:27,965
<i>Kingfisher is...</i>

811
01:06:27,965 --> 01:06:32,585
<i>a tall, well-built</i>

812
01:06:32,585 --> 01:06:34,669
<i>young man.</i>

813
01:06:34,669 --> 01:06:36,369
Who are you?

814
01:06:42,761 --> 01:06:44,545
Oh, Bo Na!

815
01:06:44,545 --> 01:06:45,789
Where are you right now?

816
01:06:45,789 --> 01:06:47,973
Well...

817
01:06:47,973 --> 01:06:50,038
Guess where I am.

818
01:06:50,705 --> 01:06:52,625
Do you know my wife?

819
01:06:52,625 --> 01:06:55,672
<i>What's your relationship with Bo Na...</i>

820
01:06:55,672 --> 01:06:58,669
<i>Nice to meet you, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.</i>

821
01:06:58,669 --> 01:07:02,538
I'm Sergei Volansky, a friend of Yoo Bo Na.

822
01:07:02,538 --> 01:07:03,945
Oh, well...

823
01:07:03,945 --> 01:07:06,205
<i>My Korean name is...</i>

824
01:07:06,205 --> 01:07:08,165
Seul Gi.

825
01:07:08,165 --> 01:07:10,149
I'm Seul Gi.

826
01:07:10,149 --> 01:07:12,505
<i>If you break your promise,</i>

827
01:07:15,049 --> 01:07:19,005
your wife and your child,

828
01:07:19,005 --> 01:07:21,738
your family could be in danger.

829
01:07:56,550 --> 01:08:00,647
[A Bona Fide Killer]

830
01:08:00,705 --> 01:08:04,745
You seem to know very little
about Bo Na, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

831
01:08:04,745 --> 01:08:07,713
I already heard it,
and I can't pretend I haven't.

832
01:08:07,713 --> 01:08:09,797
I have someone I need to protect too.

833
01:08:09,797 --> 01:08:12,438
So those two are your Achilles' heels?

834
01:08:13,861 --> 01:08:15,629
I told you not to show your face
in front of me again, didn't I?

835
01:08:15,629 --> 01:08:18,217
Because you'll end up
betraying me first anyway.

836
01:08:18,217 --> 01:08:21,269
These are the violent offenders
singled out from this year's releases.

837
01:08:21,269 --> 01:08:23,653
Dong Jin, that punk's been released.

838
01:08:23,653 --> 01:08:26,117
He already got a ridiculously light sentence,
and now he's even been paroled...

839
01:08:26,117 --> 01:08:28,265
Do you think he might do something dangerous?

840
01:08:28,265 --> 01:08:31,164
Make it cool, but it won't be easy.

841
01:08:31,164 --> 01:08:33,505
Goodbye, Tae Seong.
